  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1221 PM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nWith strengthening high pressure across West Central Texas over\nthen next several days, expect continued hot and dry conditions \ninto next early week and potentially into next weekend. \nTemperatures will remain above normal, with afternoon high \ntemperatures across the area remaining in the mid 90s to near 103 \ndegrees through next weekend. Warmest temperatures are expect \nacross the Big Country, and northern portions of the Concho \nValley and Heartland mid to late next week. Little to no \nprecipitation is expected through much of the long term forecast \nperiod. However, models have started to hint at the potential\n(slight chances) at rain showers and isolated thunderstorms making\nin into our southeastern counties later next week and weekend.",
